\f1\b\fs34 pulsingLights.cs \'96 Script Reference
\f0\b0\fs30 \
\

\f1\b Overview
\f0\b0 \
--------\
The `pulsingLights` script is used to animate the emission of a material to create a pulsing glow effect.\
\
It is used in the demo scene of the "UFO Flying Saucer (PBR)" asset and is intended solely for demonstration purposes. You can customize or remove it as needed.\
\
Note: The pulsingLights class is located in the `Hessburg` namespace.\
Be sure to include `using Hessburg;` at the top of your scripts if referencing it.\
\
Functionality\
-------------\
The script gradually changes the `_EmissionColor` property of the assigned material to simulate a pulsing light effect.\
\
On exit, it restores the original emission color of the material.\
\
Public Fields\
-------------\
- `Material ufoMaterial`: Assign the material whose emission will pulse.\
\
How It Works\
------------\
- At `Start()`: Enables emission and stores the original emission color.\
- During `Update()`: Adjusts the emission brightness using `Mathf.PingPong` over time.\
- On `Application Quit`: Restores the original emission color to avoid unintended changes in the editor.\
\
Example Use\
-----------\
This script is pre-attached and configured in the UFO demo scene.\
\
You can optionally add it to other glowing parts by assigning a material that supports `_EmissionColor`.\
\
No additional setup is required beyond assigning the material in the Inspector.\
\

